Counting pairs with sum below 2 in `[-1, 1, 2, 3, 1]`. Sorted: `[-1, 1, 1, 2, 3]`.

| lo | hi | a[lo] + a[hi] | below 2? | action | count |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | 4 | −1 + 3 = 2 | no | hi = 3 | 0 |
| 0 | 3 | −1 + 2 = 1 | yes | +3 (−1 with indices 1, 2, 3), lo = 1 | 3 |
| 1 | 3 | 1 + 2 = 3 | no | hi = 2 | 3 |
| 1 | 2 | 1 + 1 = 2 | no | hi = 1 | 3 |

Answer: 3.

```cpp
sort(a.begin(), a.end());
int lo = 0, hi = n - 1;
long long count = 0;
while (lo < hi) {
    if (a[lo] + a[hi] < target) { count += hi - lo; lo++; }
    else hi--;
}
```

Counting triangles in `[2, 2, 3, 4]` (already sorted). Fix k = 3 (length 4):

| lo | hi | a[lo] + a[hi] | > 4? | action | count |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | 2 | 2 + 3 = 5 | yes | +2 (indices 0 and 1 with 3 and 4), hi = 1 | 2 |
| 0 | 1 | 2 + 2 = 4 | no | lo = 1 | 2 |

Fix k = 2 (length 3): lo = 0, hi = 1, 2 + 2 = 4 > 3 → +1. Total **3**.

```cpp
sort(a.begin(), a.end());
long long count = 0;
for (int k = n - 1; k >= 2; k--) {
    int lo = 0, hi = k - 1;
    while (lo < hi) {
        if (a[lo] + a[hi] > a[k]) { count += hi - lo; hi--; }
        else lo++;
    }
}
```

Sorting `[2, 0, 2, 1, 1, 0]`:

| step | a | low | mid | high | a[mid] | action |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 2 0 2 1 1 0 | 0 | 0 | 5 | 2 | swap with high → 0 0 2 1 1 2, high = 4 |
| 2 | 0 0 2 1 1 2 | 0 | 0 | 4 | 0 | swap with low, low = 1, mid = 1 |
| 3 | 0 0 2 1 1 2 | 1 | 1 | 4 | 0 | swap with low, low = 2, mid = 2 |
| 4 | 0 0 2 1 1 2 | 2 | 2 | 4 | 2 | swap with high → 0 0 1 1 2 2, high = 3 |
| 5 | 0 0 1 1 2 2 | 2 | 2 | 3 | 1 | mid = 3 |
| 6 | 0 0 1 1 2 2 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 1 | mid = 4 > high: done |

